value":268,"source":{"code":"/-- If `b` divides `a` and `a` is invertible, then `b` is invertible. -/\ndef invertibleOfMul {α} [Semiring α] (k : ℕ) (b : α) :\n    ∀ (a : α) [Invertible a], a = k * b → Invertible b\n  | _, ⟨c, hc1, hc2⟩, rfl => by\n    rw [← mul_assoc] at hc1\n    rw [Nat.cast_commute k, mul_assoc, Nat.cast_commute k] at hc2\n    exact ⟨_, hc1, hc2⟩","start":182,"end":188},"axioms":["propext"]}